# ==============================================================================
# Multi-Agent Enterprise System .gitignore
# ==============================================================================
# Rules for this file:
#  * A bare name (`lib/`, `Scripts/`, `build/`) matches in EVERY folder, and Git on Windows also ignores case: `lib/` once
#    hid frontend/lib/ and `Scripts/` hid scripts/. Anything that is only an artifact of the repo root is anchored with `/`.
#  * Source, documents and test data are never ignored by extension (.docx .pdf .csv .png are real inputs in dataset/ and docs/).
#  * Ignoring a path does not untrack what is already committed: see "git rm -r --cached" at the end.
# ==============================================================================

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 1. Secrets and local configuration: never commit
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
frontend/.env
frontend/.env.*
!frontend/.env.example
docker-compose.override.yml
*.pem
*.key
*.crt
*.pfx
*.p12
*.secret
*.token
credentials.json
jwt_secret*
service_account*.json

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 2. Python
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.egg-info/
*.egg
.eggs/
.installed.cfg
MANIFEST
/build/
/dist/
/downloads/
/eggs/
/parts/
/sdist/
/var/
/wheels/
/lib/
/lib64/

# Virtual environments (a venv's own Lib/ and Scripts/ live inside these, so they need no rule)
venv/
.venv/
/env/
/ENV/
env.bak/
venv.bak/
pyvenv.cfg

# Tool caches
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.pyre/
.hypothesis/
.tox/
.nox/
.coverage
.coverage.*
coverage.xml
htmlcov/
*.cover
nosetests.xml

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 3. Frontend (Next.js 14, vitest, Playwright)
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
node_modules/
.next/
/frontend/out/
/frontend/coverage/
*.tsbuildinfo
.eslintcache
.turbo/
.vercel/
.pnp
.pnp.js
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
pnpm-debug.log*
test-results/
playwright-report/
blob-report/
playwright/.cache/
# next-env.d.ts is generated by Next but is kept in the repo on purpose (tsc needs it on a fresh checkout)

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 4. Runtime data, volumes and model weights
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
postgres_data/
redis_data/
reranker_data/
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
*.db
*.rdb
/model_cache/*
!/model_cache/.gitkeep
*.safetensors
*.onnx
*.gguf
*.pt
*.pth
*.h5
*.tflite

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 5. Logs, temporary and accidental files
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.log
logs/
*.tmp
*.temp
scratch/tmp*
# Office lock files
~$*
# accidental nested copy of the package
/src/src/
# folder created by a mistyped Windows command
/%SystemDrive%/
.system_generated/

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 6. Documentation: docs/ and every Markdown file are kept out of Git
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Files already committed (README.md, CLAUDE.md, DESIGN.md, PRODUCT.md, docs/*, reports/*.md, dataset/walkthrough_rag.md)
# stay tracked and keep showing their changes. Only NEW ones are hidden: add one on purpose with `git add -f <file>`.
# Keep this section above section 7: a later `!` rule re-includes a Markdown file.
/docs/
*.md

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 6b. Local-only folders and generated reports (kept on disk, not in the repository)
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
/legacy/
/scripts/dev/
/temp_diagrams/
/*.docx
/frontend/public/*.pdf

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 7. AI coding tools: installed packs and generated state
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Skill packs are restored from skills-lock.json (tracked); their files are not part of this project.
/.agents/
/.aider-desk/
.aider*
.gemini/
# graphify's knowledge graph is regenerated by `graphify update .` (and excluded from its own input in .graphifyignore)
/graphify-out/
# Claude Code: share the project settings, keep personal ones local
/.claude/*
!/.claude/settings.json
# Impeccable: the design record is shared (design.json, config.json, critique/ignore.md); runs and local state are not
/.impeccable/live/
/.impeccable/config.local.json
/.impeccable/critique/*
!/.impeccable/critique/ignore.md

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 8. Editors and operating systems
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
.DS_Store?
._*
.Spotlight-V100
.Trashes
ehthumbs.db
Thumbs.db
[Dd]esktop.ini

.vscode/
!.vscode/settings.json
!.vscode/tasks.json
!.vscode/launch.json
!.vscode/extensions.json
.idea/
*.sublime-workspace
*.sublime-project
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# What stays tracked on purpose (do not add rules for these)
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
#  dataset/   the corpus the RAG ingestion and CI evaluation read (pdf, docx, csv)
#  reports/   evaluation output and the RAG baseline CI compares against
#  temp_diagrams/ holds the images the report uses (docs/ and *.md are ignored by section 6)
#  frontend/lib, scripts/, migrations/versions, skills-lock.json
#
# To stop tracking files that were committed before a rule existed (history keeps them; files stay on disk):
#   git rm -r --cached .agents graphify-out .impeccable/critique/2026-10-02T02-47-04Z__frontend.md
